@startuml service_order_budget_approval
title Fluxo dinamico complementar - avaliacao da OS, aprovacao de orcamento e consulta pelo cliente
autonumber

actor "Mecanico ou Gerente" as Operator
actor "Cliente do Veiculo" as Customer
participant "Fastify / Zod" as HTTP
participant TokenActorResolver as Auth
participant UpdateServiceOrderDescription as DescriptionUC
participant AwaitBudgetApproval as AwaitUC
participant DrizzleServiceOrderRepository as OrderRepo
participant InMemoryEventBus as Bus
participant SendBudgetApprovalEmail as EmailHandler
participant DrizzleApprovalRequestRepository as ApprovalRepo
participant SmtpEmailSender as Mailer
participant DecideBudgetApproval as DecideUC
participant MoveServiceOrderToApproved as ApproveHandler
participant TrackServiceOrder as TrackUC
participant RegistryVehicleContactLookup as Contacts
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== 1. Descricao durante a Avaliacao (opcional, pode ser revisada) ==
Operator -> HTTP: PATCH /service-orders/:id/description { description } (Bearer JWT)
HTTP -> Auth: authenticate(Authorization) e verificar OS_CONCLUIR
Auth --> HTTP: ator autorizado (MECANICO ou GERENTE)
HTTP -> DescriptionUC: execute({ serviceOrderId, description })
DescriptionUC -> OrderRepo: findById(serviceOrderId)
OrderRepo -> DB: SELECT orders LEFT JOIN supply_items
DB --> OrderRepo: ServiceOrder (PENDING)
OrderRepo --> DescriptionUC: order
DescriptionUC -> DescriptionUC: order.updateDescription(description)\nvalida PENDING, remove espacos das extremidades e rejeita texto vazio
DescriptionUC -> OrderRepo: save(order)
OrderRepo -> DB: TX: persiste orders.description e incrementa version\nsem nova entrada de historico (status permanece PENDING)
DB --> OrderRepo: COMMIT
DescriptionUC --> HTTP: { serviceOrderId, description }
HTTP --> Operator: HTTP 200

note over HTTP,OrderRepo
  Sem token/ator valido: HTTP 401; sem OS_CONCLUIR: HTTP 403.
  OS inexistente: HTTP 404; descricao vazia ou OS fora de PENDING: HTTP 400.
  Conflito de versao na persistencia: HTTP 409.
end note

== 2. Envio da OS para Aprovacao de Orcamento ==
Operator -> HTTP: POST /service-orders/:id/awaiting-approval { valueCents?, description? } (Bearer JWT)
HTTP -> Auth: authenticate(Authorization) e verificar OS_CONCLUIR
Auth --> HTTP: ator autorizado
HTTP -> AwaitUC: execute({ serviceOrderId, valueCents, description })
AwaitUC -> OrderRepo: findById(serviceOrderId)
OrderRepo -> DB: SELECT orders LEFT JOIN supply_items
DB --> OrderRepo: ServiceOrder (PENDING)
AwaitUC -> AwaitUC: order.setValueCents(valueCents) se informado e valida valor\norder.updateDescription(description) se informada\ncria Budget(order.valueCents) e chama order.awaitApproval(budget.id)
AwaitUC -> OrderRepo: save(order, budget)
OrderRepo -> DB: TX: persiste orders (AWAITING_APPROVAL, value_cents, description),\nbudgets (PENDING) e order_status_history
DB --> OrderRepo: COMMIT
AwaitUC -> Bus: publish([OrderAwaitingApproval])
Bus -> EmailHandler: handle(OrderAwaitingApproval)
EmailHandler -> ApprovalRepo: issue(ApprovalRequest com tokenHash e budgetVersion)
ApprovalRepo -> DB: TX: revoga anteriores e INSERT approval_requests
EmailHandler -> Mailer: send(e-mail HTML/texto com order.description, valor\ne /orcamento/:token?acao=aprovar|recusar)
EmailHandler -> ApprovalRepo: markSent(request.id)
Bus --> AwaitUC: publish concluido
AwaitUC --> HTTP: { status: "AWAITING_APPROVAL" }
HTTP --> Operator: HTTP 200

note over AwaitUC,Mailer
  description omitida preserva o texto salvo na avaliacao.
  Apos o envio (AWAITING_APPROVAL), a edicao da descricao fica bloqueada.
  O hash budgetVersion inclui a descricao, o valor e os itens da OS.
  A pagina /orcamento/:token confirma a decisao; a descricao esta no e-mail.
end note

== 3. Decisao do Cliente via Token ==
Customer -> HTTP: POST /budget-approvals/decide { token, decision, rejectionReason? }
HTTP -> DecideUC: execute(input)
DecideUC -> ApprovalRepo: findByTokenHash(sha256(token))
ApprovalRepo -> DB: SELECT approval_requests
DB --> ApprovalRepo: ApprovalRequest ativo
DecideUC -> OrderRepo: findById(orderId) + BudgetRepository.findById(budgetId)
DecideUC -> DecideUC: valida AWAITING_APPROVAL, budgetVersion, request.decide() e budget.approve()|reject()
DecideUC -> ApprovalRepo: decide(request, budget, order.version)

alt decision == "approved"
  ApprovalRepo -> DB: TX: SELECT orders FOR UPDATE, UPDATE approval_requests (used_at), UPDATE budgets (APPROVED)
  DB --> ApprovalRepo: COMMIT
  DecideUC -> Bus: publish([BudgetApproved])
  Bus -> ApproveHandler: handle(BudgetApproved)
  ApproveHandler -> OrderRepo: findById(serviceOrderId)
  ApproveHandler -> ApproveHandler: order.approve()
  ApproveHandler -> OrderRepo: save(order)
  OrderRepo -> DB: TX: UPDATE orders (APPROVED), INSERT order_status_history
  DB --> OrderRepo: COMMIT
else decision == "rejected"
  ApprovalRepo -> DB: TX: UPDATE approval_requests, UPDATE budgets (REJECTED), UPDATE orders (REJECTED), INSERT order_status_history
  DB --> ApprovalRepo: COMMIT
end

DecideUC --> HTTP: { status: "decided", decision }
HTTP --> Customer: HTTP 200

note over ApprovalRepo,OrderRepo
  Se o mesmo token ja decidido receber novamente a mesma decision,
  DecideBudgetApproval retorna { status: "already_decided", decision } (idempotencia).
  Se o orcamento/OS tiver sido modificado (budgetVersion divergente),
  retorna HTTP 400 (BudgetChangedError).
end note

== 4. Consulta do Andamento pelo Cliente (sem login) ==
Customer -> HTTP: POST /service-orders/:id/tracking { document } (rate-limit 10/min por IP)
HTTP -> TrackUC: execute({ serviceOrderId, document })
TrackUC -> OrderRepo: findById(serviceOrderId)
OrderRepo -> DB: SELECT orders
TrackUC -> Contacts: findByVehicleId(order.vehicleId)
Contacts -> DB: SELECT veiculo e cliente
alt CPF/CNPJ informado = titular do veiculo
  TrackUC -> OrderRepo: findStatusHistory(serviceOrderId)
  OrderRepo -> DB: SELECT order_status_history
  TrackUC --> HTTP: { serviceOrderId, description, status, valueCents, history[{ status, recordedAt }] }
  HTTP --> Customer: HTTP 200
else OS inexistente ou documento divergente
  TrackUC --> HTTP: ServiceOrderNotFoundError
  HTTP --> Customer: HTTP 404 (nao revela se a OS existe)
end
@enduml
